WEBVTT

00:10.790 --> 00:11.580
Oh!

00:11.750 --> 00:13.670
Anna! Great timing!

00:14.130 --> 00:16.000
These Valentine's chocolates are for you.

00:16.000 --> 00:16.830
These too!

00:17.290 --> 00:18.460
Thanks.

00:18.960 --> 00:19.830
So cute!

00:19.830 --> 00:21.330
Just adorable!

00:24.790 --> 00:25.580
Swivel!

00:25.880 --> 00:27.580
Maybe I'll do one more pass.

00:27.580 --> 00:29.250
You've already made five round trips!

00:29.250 --> 00:30.290
Hmm...

00:32.420 --> 00:34.170
Look at how many I got!

00:34.170 --> 00:36.580
Yeah, great for you.

00:36.580 --> 00:37.750
What about you?

00:37.750 --> 00:39.330
Me? I got some from my mom...

00:39.330 --> 00:40.500
A day like any other...
Me? I got some from my mom...<b></b>

00:40.500 --> 00:41.210
A day like any other...

00:41.670 --> 00:42.830
You must be so happy!

00:42.830 --> 00:44.130
February fourteenth.
I mean, she's my mom...<b></b>

00:44.130 --> 00:44.710
I mean, she's my mom...

00:44.710 --> 00:46.210
Yup yup, that's great.

00:46.540 --> 00:49.920
Let's call for an end to obligatory chocolates!

00:49.920 --> 00:54.080
We can't let any more poor guys
go gettin' the wrong idea!

00:49.920 --> 00:55.380
<b>Year 2 Class 3</b>

00:55.540 --> 00:58.460
Okay. Snooze you lose!

01:01.710 --> 01:03.290
Aren't we calling for an end to those?

01:04.170 --> 01:05.670
They're like pigeons.

01:07.710 --> 01:09.130
Hurry up and clear this out.

01:09.130 --> 01:09.880
You take one?

01:09.880 --> 01:10.540
Nope.

01:10.540 --> 01:11.460
That's yours, then.

01:11.460 --> 01:12.170
No, thanks!

01:12.170 --> 01:14.790
Figured, that's why I put them all on your desk.

01:14.790 --> 01:15.460
Huh?

01:15.460 --> 01:16.170
Hmm?

01:17.540 --> 01:19.420
Yamada!

01:20.250 --> 01:22.380
I'm a boy for the day, y'know!

01:22.380 --> 01:23.880
You're such a glutton!

01:26.210 --> 01:29.080
Dude, look! This nut is shaped like a heart!

01:29.080 --> 01:31.080
Think this is some secret sign?!

01:31.080 --> 01:32.420
Gimme a break.

01:32.420 --> 01:34.000
I shouldn't have gave 'em anything.

01:34.000 --> 01:34.830
Seriously.

01:34.830 --> 01:37.080
Only takes one little chocolate to give the wrong idea.

01:37.080 --> 01:38.670
Guys are pure of heart like that!

01:38.830 --> 01:40.130
Same goes for you, right?

01:40.130 --> 01:41.960
You're a pure, Cinderella-like guy!

01:41.960 --> 01:42.830
Shut up.

03:15.000 --> 03:16.960
<b>Library</b>

03:17.130 --> 03:18.880
Let's play shogi today!

03:19.080 --> 03:20.790
I don't even really know the rules.

03:20.790 --> 03:23.750
That's fine, we're only playing Tirol Chocolate shogi.

03:23.750 --> 03:24.500
Ta-da!

03:24.500 --> 03:25.960
Then I DEFINITELY don't know the rules.

03:34.040 --> 03:35.960
I never saw that coming...

03:35.960 --> 03:37.040
Saw what?

03:38.080 --> 03:39.630
You say it, too.

03:39.630 --> 03:41.290
"N-never saw-"

03:41.290 --> 03:42.290
Not now!

03:42.290 --> 03:43.460
Then when?

03:46.960 --> 03:50.130
Could have all the time in the world and
I still wouldn't get this.

03:50.960 --> 03:51.750
Huh?

03:52.130 --> 03:52.920
So how do we w-

03:52.920 --> 03:53.830
You win.

03:53.830 --> 03:54.540
Huh?

03:55.000 --> 03:55.960
Here.

03:57.830 --> 04:00.670
Winner takes all the pieces.

04:00.670 --> 04:01.960
That's the rule.

04:10.880 --> 04:12.290
Now's the time...

04:14.080 --> 04:15.580
What?

04:15.790 --> 04:16.830
Thanks...

04:18.290 --> 04:20.750
<b>Library</b>

04:21.210 --> 04:22.210
Chocolate...

04:23.210 --> 04:24.670
Chocolate...

04:25.460 --> 04:26.960
These are chocolates.

04:26.960 --> 04:28.880
They definitely are.

04:29.670 --> 04:31.080
Show me your chocolate!

04:32.880 --> 04:36.290
Yours has no heart,
it's just an obligatory one! Okay!

04:36.290 --> 04:38.290
I definitely don't want to get the wrong idea like him!

04:38.670 --> 04:42.460
Shoulda just went with ones that said,
"OBLIGATORY" on 'em.

04:42.460 --> 04:46.330
Can't just go giving chocolates, huh?

04:46.330 --> 04:48.670
Gotta make it clear how you feel.

04:54.580 --> 04:55.830
Chocolate...

04:56.420 --> 05:01.080
More than that, the fact she'd even
give away any snack is a miracle.

05:01.080 --> 05:04.880
Is this just her being unpredictable again?

05:05.540 --> 05:06.790
How am I s'posed to run like this?!

05:10.960 --> 05:12.250
This is for you.

05:12.250 --> 05:13.250
Th-

05:14.080 --> 05:15.290
Thanks...

05:18.670 --> 05:19.750
I'm jealous...

05:19.750 --> 05:21.540
You can't get all the chocolate, y'know.

05:22.210 --> 05:23.330
That's not what I mean!

05:24.460 --> 05:27.170
She's extra unpredictable today.

05:31.710 --> 05:35.290
Why make a big deal about giving them out at school?

05:35.500 --> 05:41.500
I mean, Hara and Kanzaki walk
together and go on d-dates, right?

05:42.000 --> 05:43.420
She could give 'em to him whenever.

05:43.420 --> 05:44.830
There are plenty of hours in the day.

05:47.830 --> 05:49.670
School is a place of learning.

05:49.670 --> 05:51.130
And no, I'm not just jealous.

05:51.630 --> 05:52.920
Later, then.

05:53.380 --> 05:54.290
Huh?

05:54.580 --> 05:55.710
Gimme a lift.

05:59.880 --> 06:01.540
Riding sideways is scary!

06:02.500 --> 06:04.080
Slow down a little.

06:05.670 --> 06:07.750
There are plenty of hours in the day.

06:12.000 --> 06:14.290
We're at it again, huh?

06:15.420 --> 06:19.630
I thought I was dead when we
rode by that police box last time.

06:20.380 --> 06:21.750
I didn't even notice!

06:21.750 --> 06:25.170
I thought about telling you to get off, but...

06:25.290 --> 06:27.960
<b>Dangerous - Don't Touch!</b>

06:25.830 --> 06:27.920
Afraid of a little change, huh?

06:28.170 --> 06:30.920
I couldn't after you said that.

06:31.130 --> 06:35.330
<b>ONE WAY</b>

06:31.130 --> 06:35.330
<b>Except for Bicycles</b>

06:31.290 --> 06:33.170
Did I really say that?

06:33.170 --> 06:35.210
Pretty sure those were your exact words.

06:36.380 --> 06:39.380
You live for change, so you wouldn't get it.

06:39.710 --> 06:40.960
True.

06:44.960 --> 06:48.580
But, I think I understand now...

06:51.170 --> 06:53.830
Maybe it's 'cause I'm so happy now...

07:01.040 --> 07:03.080
N-no! I still need more!

07:03.540 --> 07:05.540
I mean, I'm still hungry.

07:12.960 --> 07:15.210
T-this stuff sure is pricey, huh?

07:15.460 --> 07:18.000
<b>Heart Choco Bun</b>

07:15.460 --> 07:18.000
<b>(with Belgian chocolate)</b>

07:15.460 --> 07:18.000
<b>Juicy Meat Bun</b>

07:15.460 --> 07:18.000
<b>(with Japanese Sangen pork)</b>

07:20.710 --> 07:22.080
You got the chocolate bun?

07:22.080 --> 07:23.080
Mhmm.

07:24.330 --> 07:27.420
Didn't you get a bunch of
chocolate from the year one girls?

07:27.420 --> 07:30.130
It's fine! I can eat chocolate forever!

07:31.040 --> 07:33.000
That bag's full of obviously obligatory chocolates.

07:33.000 --> 07:33.790
Swish!

07:34.080 --> 07:34.710
Don't!

07:34.710 --> 07:35.630
Wasn't gonna!

07:38.580 --> 07:40.330
So did you...?

07:41.040 --> 07:42.500
No, uhh...

07:43.500 --> 07:47.670
What sort of chocolate would make
you think it actually meant something?

07:48.170 --> 07:50.040
That's a tough one...

07:53.500 --> 07:56.290
I might not know unless I was told so.

08:01.210 --> 08:02.880
It'd be tough otherwise...

08:08.880 --> 08:12.460
Oh, I guess some people might get
the wrong idea if it was heart shaped!

08:17.130 --> 08:19.040
According to Adachi, at least.

08:19.040 --> 08:19.710
Ichikawa.

08:19.710 --> 08:20.420
Huh?

08:20.420 --> 08:21.330
What?!

08:23.710 --> 08:24.710
What the...?

08:25.460 --> 08:26.580
You can have it.

08:26.580 --> 08:27.790
Thanks...

08:32.670 --> 08:33.710
Wha?!

08:42.080 --> 08:43.330
Got some on your face.

08:57.330 --> 08:58.420
Bye-bye!

09:02.420 --> 09:06.750
For a second, I think I really let my hopes up.

09:07.580 --> 09:10.380
I might not know unless I was told so.

09:40.290 --> 09:41.960
Y-you're still here...

09:43.710 --> 09:45.750
C'mon, you can do this!

09:46.330 --> 09:47.460
Hey.

09:48.380 --> 09:49.460
This is for you.

09:51.080 --> 09:53.250
Back in class you said...

09:53.710 --> 09:56.080
...you're a guy today.

09:58.330 --> 10:00.630
I'm a boy for the day, y'know!

10:03.540 --> 10:04.290
Later, then.

10:04.290 --> 10:05.330
No, w-

10:21.830 --> 10:22.540
Good!

10:22.540 --> 10:23.460
That's it!

10:23.460 --> 10:24.960
Good thinking.

10:24.960 --> 10:26.130
Think that was the right move.

10:26.130 --> 10:27.500
This is Yamada we're talking about.

10:31.750 --> 10:33.210
No, that was definitely weird!

10:33.210 --> 10:36.920
Why did I pick something called,
"Melty Kiss" of all things?!

10:41.540 --> 10:43.000
I'm afraid to look...

10:43.580 --> 10:44.460
What?

10:53.670 --> 10:55.670
February fourteenth.

10:56.250 --> 10:57.750
Hey!

10:58.040 --> 11:00.170
7:26 PM.

11:05.040 --> 11:09.330
Just, y'know, thought I'd change
Wantaro's walking course.

11:09.500 --> 11:09.960
Hey.

11:11.170 --> 11:13.880
And then I realized we were close by.

11:14.670 --> 11:16.080
Let's talk.

11:16.080 --> 11:17.170
'Kay...

11:20.420 --> 11:21.580
Wanna hold the lead?

11:21.580 --> 11:22.880
Sure that's okay?

11:28.040 --> 11:29.580
Be sure to hold it down.

11:31.750 --> 11:33.130
There you have it.

11:33.130 --> 11:34.170
Right...

11:37.380 --> 11:38.330
Okay!

11:38.710 --> 11:39.960
Time to gamble!

11:41.790 --> 11:43.750
The hot cocoa I want,

11:43.750 --> 11:46.420
and the black coffee I definitely don't,

11:46.420 --> 11:49.330
pressed at the same time for the thrill of it!

11:49.330 --> 11:50.920
You call that gambling?

11:50.920 --> 11:51.670
Go!

11:52.460 --> 11:54.630
<b>Sugarless</b>

11:52.460 --> 11:54.630
<b>Black</b>

11:52.460 --> 11:54.630
<b>No sugar</b>

11:57.080 --> 12:00.130
I pressed them at the same time!

12:02.960 --> 12:04.630
Here, you can have this.

12:04.630 --> 12:05.710
What?

12:05.710 --> 12:06.710
Thanks...

12:07.080 --> 12:09.080
<b>Meguro Ward</b>

12:07.080 --> 12:09.080
<b>Senzoku Station Plaza</b>

12:10.670 --> 12:18.830
So then Chii was like, "Leave those bees be!"

12:18.830 --> 12:21.210
A-and then, let's see...

12:21.210 --> 12:23.330
You're acting really weird today.

12:23.670 --> 12:24.830
Something's off.

12:27.920 --> 12:29.130
I'm always weird.

12:29.130 --> 12:29.790
True.

12:29.790 --> 12:31.330
Hey now!

12:31.540 --> 12:33.170
You said it yourself.

12:33.170 --> 12:37.710
Chii's always calling me weird,
but she's not around so I said it for her.

12:39.330 --> 12:40.790
You cold?

12:40.790 --> 12:42.170
I'm fine.

12:42.500 --> 12:44.040
Thanks for the chocolate!

12:44.040 --> 12:45.380
Oh, yeah...

12:45.380 --> 12:47.210
Sure is warm this year, huh?

12:47.210 --> 12:48.380
Yeah...

12:48.880 --> 12:49.960
Guess it's not gonna snow again.

12:49.960 --> 12:51.040
What are we doing here?
Guess it's not gonna snow again.<b></b>

12:51.040 --> 12:51.880
What are we doing here?

12:52.960 --> 12:54.750
I-Ichi...

12:57.420 --> 13:00.290
Did you get any chocolate today?

13:00.750 --> 13:02.080
Other than from family.

13:02.080 --> 13:02.880
Huh?

13:03.000 --> 13:04.000
Here.

13:04.330 --> 13:05.880
That's the rule.

13:05.880 --> 13:07.080
Now's the time...

13:07.580 --> 13:08.750
You can have it.

13:11.500 --> 13:12.500
Nope.

13:13.580 --> 13:14.790
Yeah?

13:15.960 --> 13:19.920
D-did you give anyone any?

13:21.500 --> 13:23.580
That's safe to ask, right?

13:24.880 --> 13:29.380
Nope. I decided not to give out any obligatory ones.

13:29.790 --> 13:31.460
Oh, yeah?

13:32.040 --> 13:32.920
Hmm?

13:33.210 --> 13:36.040
Winner takes all the pieces.

13:36.040 --> 13:37.130
You can have it.

13:38.540 --> 13:43.580
Well, I agree with Adachi that we should
get rid of obligatory chocolates.

13:43.580 --> 13:46.460
All it does is give poor guys the wrong idea.

13:46.460 --> 13:47.460
Is that bitter?

13:49.130 --> 13:51.960
I was lying when I said I didn't like sweet stuff.

13:54.540 --> 13:55.670
Well then...

14:08.960 --> 14:13.040
I-I made it too sweet, see...

14:14.710 --> 14:15.580
Li-?

14:16.170 --> 14:17.380
Snap!

14:27.580 --> 14:28.750
Thanks.

14:29.960 --> 14:31.170
It's okay.

14:34.830 --> 14:38.540
It's okay to get the wrong idea.

14:48.040 --> 14:49.250
Yamada's...

14:54.960 --> 14:55.880
Huh?!

14:57.080 --> 14:58.210
What?!

15:00.630 --> 15:02.790
I couldn't get it right...

15:03.460 --> 15:04.290
Any of it...

15:09.580 --> 15:11.460
This is actually good!

15:12.130 --> 15:15.500
No, I mean, it's really good!

15:17.790 --> 15:19.080
Well, then...

15:19.830 --> 15:21.580
...gimme another.

15:42.920 --> 15:44.330
Yamada...

15:47.670 --> 15:49.630
<b>Yamada...</b>

15:47.880 --> 15:49.170
Yamada...

16:01.130 --> 16:02.830
<b>...Likes...</b>

16:01.290 --> 16:02.460
...likes...

16:05.790 --> 16:08.710
<b>Yamada Likes...</b>

16:26.000 --> 16:28.130
What's with the face?

16:28.130 --> 16:30.460
What am I gonna give her for White Day?

16:30.460 --> 16:32.170
That's still a month away.

16:32.170 --> 16:33.170
No.

16:34.170 --> 16:36.500
You could say we only have one month left.

16:38.290 --> 16:41.540
That's right. I got chocolate from Yamada.

16:42.080 --> 16:43.630
I sure did.

16:43.960 --> 16:52.880
<b>Best Seller</b>

16:43.960 --> 16:52.880
<b>The Boy and One Month</b>

16:44.250 --> 16:46.710
Am I going to be able to give her something

16:46.710 --> 16:48.710
good back for White Day a month from now?

16:48.710 --> 16:52.290
What's important now is me and this one month.

16:53.000 --> 16:56.130
All you got were the chocolates Sekine gave everyone.

16:56.130 --> 16:58.290
But, mine had a heart-shaped nut in it!

16:58.290 --> 17:00.420
Girls want you to pick up on that stuff.

17:00.420 --> 17:03.000
You should set him straight, Moe.
There's always the chance.<b></b>

17:03.380 --> 17:08.500
I'll let you figure out what it meant!

17:08.670 --> 17:09.670
That's just cruel.

17:09.670 --> 17:10.630
I knew it!

17:10.630 --> 17:13.330
I'd really love some ear pods.

17:13.330 --> 17:15.380
Y'know, I really wanna get her
something that makes her scream:

17:15.380 --> 17:16.250
"You're amazing!"

17:16.250 --> 17:19.790
"What good taste!" "Take me!"
"I'll even take runner up!"

17:20.040 --> 17:21.670
Guy wants a whole fan club.

17:21.670 --> 17:24.000
This calls for sexy lingerie!

17:24.000 --> 17:25.630
What "calls" for that?

17:25.630 --> 17:29.460
I got handmade chocolate,
so maybe it should be handmade lingerie!

17:29.460 --> 17:31.380
You're digging your own grave.

17:31.460 --> 17:34.920
I might go for an all-you-can-eat snack buffet.

17:34.920 --> 17:37.080
Oh, that's a pretty good idea.

17:37.080 --> 17:37.880
Hmm?!

17:38.580 --> 17:40.920
Inviting her out is the hard part, though...

17:43.710 --> 17:46.330
Wait, you got chocolate?!

17:46.330 --> 17:47.040
Shoot!

17:47.630 --> 17:50.500
Well, I guess, yeah...

17:50.500 --> 17:52.540
No point in lying.

17:55.750 --> 17:57.960
Whatever! Bet she's ugly!

18:08.330 --> 18:13.080
I mean, if you don't even like her,
who cares what you get her?

18:13.080 --> 18:16.040
I like the girls that like me.

18:16.040 --> 18:18.710
Better to have as many chances as you can.

18:18.710 --> 18:20.290
Too bad you have none.

18:20.500 --> 18:24.580
I realized I don't know a thing 'bout Sekine.

18:24.580 --> 18:28.290
That's what scares me. Can't half-ass this.

18:28.290 --> 18:29.750
Sure taking this seriously.

18:29.750 --> 18:31.960
So where are we even going?

18:31.960 --> 18:32.830
Oh!

18:33.330 --> 18:34.290
Hey.

18:35.880 --> 18:36.580
Huh?

18:36.750 --> 18:41.960
<b>ADACHI</b>

18:36.830 --> 18:39.710
Nanjo here's on the student committee with me.

18:39.710 --> 18:41.670
What? This guy's fading out of existence!

18:42.080 --> 18:45.540
He's got all the ladies,
so we should ask him for advice!

18:45.540 --> 18:47.210
He still exists...

18:47.630 --> 18:49.330
I don't really get all the ladies.

18:49.330 --> 18:50.960
Like I believe that.

18:50.960 --> 18:55.000
I just have a sense for when I have a chance.

18:55.000 --> 18:57.750
Can tell when the mood's right.

18:57.750 --> 18:59.170
No, you can't.

19:03.920 --> 19:09.000
This guy got some Valentine chocolate too,
so we were wondering what to give back.

19:10.040 --> 19:12.920
Oh, got some, did ya?

19:14.580 --> 19:17.670
I don't really know what my girl likes, though.

19:17.670 --> 19:20.460
Think I should figure that out, first?

19:20.460 --> 19:22.580
Nah. No point in that.

19:22.580 --> 19:26.380
Guys and girls can never really know each other.

19:26.380 --> 19:28.460
Yeah, guess you're right.

19:28.460 --> 19:29.580
You think?

19:31.580 --> 19:33.380
They're a whole different animal.

19:34.380 --> 19:37.290
Different upbringing, different tastes, different values.

19:37.290 --> 19:42.000
But, when you get to know them,
you find what you have in common.

19:42.000 --> 19:46.460
Finding what you can share or
understand about each other, I say.

19:49.080 --> 19:52.710
So uhh, what kinda presents should we get?

19:54.710 --> 19:57.210
What about lingerie or something?

19:57.830 --> 20:00.000
Oh, I knew it!

20:00.000 --> 20:02.500
I'm sure they'll love it.

20:02.920 --> 20:04.380
Right, Ichihara?

20:04.380 --> 20:06.210
What a lame trap.

20:08.250 --> 20:11.040
I knew he was the right guy to ask!

20:11.040 --> 20:12.130
You think?

20:13.210 --> 20:17.040
You help me learn and realize more stuff than he does.

20:18.290 --> 20:20.790
H-hey, you're not gonna win me over, here!

20:21.250 --> 20:22.540
Gotta get to practice!

20:24.830 --> 20:26.380
I'm going home.

20:28.540 --> 20:29.500
Oh!

20:29.880 --> 20:31.500
Hey!

20:31.710 --> 20:33.460
Hey!

20:34.540 --> 20:35.880
Cut it...

21:01.750 --> 21:05.330
I-I... like... Ya-

21:06.420 --> 21:07.580
Hang on, now!

21:18.080 --> 21:19.710
Oh! Bye!
